> Configure project :core:crypto
w: ⚠️ Cross Compilation with Cinterop Not Supported in Project 'crypto'
In project 'crypto', cross compilation to target 'iosArm64' has been disabled because it contains cinterops: 'rawSodium' which cannot be processed on host 'linux_x64'.
Cinterop libraries require platform-specific native toolchains that aren't available on the current host system.
Solutions:
 * Remove the cinterop dependencies 'rawSodium' from target 'iosArm64'
 * Build on a compatible host platform for this target/cinterop combination
 * To disable klib cross compilation entirely, add 'kotlin.native.enableKlibsCrossCompilation=false' to your Gradle properties

w: ⚠️ Cross Compilation with Cinterop Not Supported in Project 'crypto'
In project 'crypto', cross compilation to target 'iosSimulatorArm64' has been disabled because it contains cinterops: 'rawSodium' which cannot be processed on host 'linux_x64'.
Cinterop libraries require platform-specific native toolchains that aren't available on the current host system.
Solutions:
 * Remove the cinterop dependencies 'rawSodium' from target 'iosSimulatorArm64'
 * Build on a compatible host platform for this target/cinterop combination
 * To disable klib cross compilation entirely, add 'kotlin.native.enableKlibsCrossCompilation=false' to your Gradle properties

